Removing the mis-scaled/conflicting smoothness objective will let the optimizer trade spectrum match vs the physically relevant second-difference smoothness (smoothness_v2). Evidence: spectrum_match mean = 0.823 ±0.073 (best 0.9260) improved strongly, but smoothness_v2 mean dropped from 0.1673 → 0.0042 (now 0.0042 ±0.0041), while "smoothness" has mean 468.1 ±403.3 (range 49.5–1542.97) despite documented [0,1] — indicating a likely scorer implementation/scale bug that is dominating selection.

